  "body": "First slice of #620: machine files for the **Tormach 24R** and **xsTECH Pro** routers. The plain xsTECH Router waits for its manual.\n\n## Sources (cited in `docs/decisions/620-tormach-routers.md`)\n- **24R:** Tormach UM10564 0826A §2.2, Machine Specifications.\n- **xsTECH Pro:** the xsTECH Pro spec sheet (2026) and UM10859 (xsTECH Pro CE manual) §2.\n\n## What changed\n- **`assets/machines/tormach-24r.mch`:**\n  - X 24.75 / Y 55.75 / Z 6.7 in;\n  - 1.5 kW electrospindle, **10000-24000 rpm**;\n  - 200 IPM on every axis;\n  - ATC left unstated (optional, no station count given).\n- **`assets/machines/tormach-xstech-pro.mch`:**\n  - X 10.2 (with the standard tool changer);\n  - **Y 7.9** (the CE manual) over the US sheet's 9.3, and Z 6.3 over the CE manual's 6.5. Where the documents disagree, the smaller travel is used, since it can only refuse a move, never let a bad one through;\n  - 0.35 kW, max 20000 rpm with no minimum stated;\n  - a 4-station ATC (T5 and up is refused);\n  - **no feed ceiling stated**, because none is documented.\n- **Both machines:**\n  - rigid tapping false (not documented), so a tapping cycle is refused by name;\n  - no coolant (none documented), so a Flood op is refused by name;\n  - safe retract Z0, the Tormach convention.\n- **Registration:** added to `MACHINES`. Both get the Tormach PathPilot mill post, as the Tormach mills do.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `tormach_routers` (4):**\n  - the documents' figures;\n  - the xsTECH Pro states no feed ceiling;\n  - both post through PathPilot (S18000, G20, no warnings);\n  - a **5000 rpm job is refused on the 24R** (\"below the machine's 10000\"), and the same job at 18000 posts.\n- **Gate:** machine 32, machine_library, tormach_machines, tormach_safe_retract, tormach_post, posting and conformance pass. Clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nA PathPilot Hub run of a profile on a router.\n\nChangelog: Tormach 24R and xsTECH Pro router machine files (PathPilot post; the 24R refuses spindle speeds below its 10000 rpm floor) (#620)\n\nRefs #620\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
